00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.320
So, here on the reel you can see the top end,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.840
a really beautiful sample  of research quality Platinum.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:20.520
- Platinum is a very heavy metal and it is like silver and gold.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.400
It’s a metal which does not  easily react with the oxygen in the air.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.400
So, if you make jewelry out of it, it stays nice and shiny and looks nice.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.960
Platinum, unlike gold is, has a silvery color which some people like.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.920
You can make alloys of silver and... of Gold and Platinum

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.680
which will have different colors of yellow depending on your taste.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.480
- Platinum is a very very precious metal. It's of very very high value

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.920
not just for jewelry, but also for the production 

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.400
of auto-catalytic converters and other chemical processes.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.200
This wire here is very very fine. It's 0.01 millimeters in diameter

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.120
and it is used to study vapor phase and gas phase chemistries.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:12.210
- Platinum is found in a number of places around the world, for example, in South Africa.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.800
But, it's of very small amount, each ton of rock

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.280
may have as a little of 7 grams of Platinum in it.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.560
So, you have to break an awful lot of rock to get this material.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.180
In recent years,  Platinum has become very important 

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.360
in catalysts in cars. The catalytic converters

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.400
and so, more and more cars, infact all cars now have Platinum 

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.320
in their catalytic converters. And, if we are going to go to

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:49.360
Hydrogen powered cars using fuel cells, these will probably also need Platinum.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.520
In fact, that is a considerable question, whether there is enough Platinum 

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.640
in the world to frill the uses we want to put it is to.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.530
This is 1 gram, there. 1 gram of Platinum.

